---
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// The photo deck renders only when real images exist in public/photos/.
// Any image file in that directory is picked up, sorted by name. Alt text
// comes from photoAlt below, matched by position; update it when the photos
// change so the descriptions stay accurate.
const photoDir = path.join(process.cwd(), 'public', 'photos');
const photos = fs.existsSync(photoDir)
  ? fs
      .readdirSync(photoDir)
      .filter((f) => /\.(jpe?g|png|webp)$/i.test(f))
      .sort()
  : [];
const photoAlt = [
  'Javier with his family',
  'Javier with his family',
  'Rambi and Coco',
  'Javier with his family',
  'Javier with his dogs in Los Angeles',
];
---

<Base
  title="About · Javier Saldana"
  description="Platform engineer working on identity and authorization infrastructure. How I got here, and what I do when I'm not working."
>
  <div class="page">
    <p class="label">About</p>
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p class="meta resume-line">
      <a href="/Javier_Saldana_Resume.pdf">Resume (PDF)</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/saldanaj27">GitHub</a> ·
      <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/javier-saldana27">LinkedIn</a> ·
      <a href="mailto:saldanaj27@gmail.com">saldanaj27@gmail.com</a>
    </p>

    <p>
      I'm a platform engineer working on identity and authorization
      infrastructure. Every professional system I have shipped is a shared
      primitive consumed by other engineering teams, including authentication
      services, authorization policy distribution, Kubernetes operators with
      CRDs as declarative APIs, and a UID generation service. My users are other
      engineers, which is the part of the job I like most.
    </p>

    <h2>Outside work</h2>

    <p>
      I'm Peruvian-American, originally from Los Angeles, and moved to New York
      for college in 2018. I'm the second in my family to go to college, after
      an older sister who is now in residency. Home is my parents, my sister,
      and two dogs I adore, Rambi and Coco, both past sixteen and both still in
      Los Angeles.
    </p>

    {
      photos.length > 0 && (
        <figure class="family">
          <div class="deck" role="group" aria-label="Family photos">
            {photos.map((file, idx) => (
              <img
                src={`/photos/${file}`}
                alt={photoAlt[idx] ?? 'Family photo'}
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
              />
            ))}
          </div>
        </figure>
      )
    }

    <p>
      I'm a college football fan, specifically USC. I did not go to USC. I grew
      up in LA cheering for them, which is the whole explanation and, I'd argue,
      enough of one.
    </p>

    <p>
      Those who know me best know I spend a lot of my time playing Minesweeper.
      It's the same appeal that pulled me into computer science, a constrained
      board with incomplete information and a solution that yields to reasoning
      instead of speed (though for the record, my time to beat on a 16x30 board
      is 69.12 seconds). I also play soccer, and I'm working on running more
      consistently.
    </p>

    <p>
      Fun fact, I was once a licensed scuba diver (stopped after realizing I am
      afraid of the deep ocean).
    </p>

    <p>
      Another fun fact, I've visited all seven wonders of the world with my
      family.
    </p>

    <h2>What I'm looking for</h2>
    <p>
      Platform services, distributed systems, and infrastructure that other
      engineers build on, including internal developer platforms, orchestration,
      and AI infrastructure. I'm most useful on teams whose customers are other
      engineering teams, and I'm deliberately open to domains beyond identity.
      If that sounds like your team,
      <a href="mailto:saldanaj27@gmail.com">say hello</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <style>
    /* The global wrap is wider than the reading measure, which left a much
       bigger gutter on the right than the left. Center the measure instead. */
    .page {
      max-width: var(--measure);
      margin-inline: auto;
    }
    .page > * + * {
      margin-top: 1.25rem;
    }
    .resume-line {
      margin-top: 0.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    /* Photo deck: overlapping cards that cycle focus on a timer, like a hand
       of cards being fanned. Hover or focus lifts one to the front. Degrades
       to a plain row when JS is off, and holds still under reduced motion. */
    .family {
      margin-top: 1.75rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
    }
    .deck {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      align-items: center;
      padding: 0.75rem 0;
    }
    .deck img {
      width: clamp(6.5rem, 19%, 9.5rem);
      aspect-ratio: 3 / 4;
      object-fit: cover;
      border: 1px solid var(--rule);
      border-radius: 4px;
      background: var(--bg-subtle);
      box-shadow: 0 2px 10px rgb(0 0 0 / 12%);
      transition:
        transform 420ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 0.61, 0.36, 1),
        box-shadow 420ms ease,
        filter 420ms ease;
      transform-origin: center bottom;
      filter: saturate(0.92);
      will-change: transform;
    }
    .deck img + img {
      margin-left: -1.75rem;
    }
    .deck img:nth-child(1) {
      rotate: -6deg;
    }
    .deck img:nth-child(2) {
      rotate: -2.5deg;
    }
    .deck img:nth-child(3) {
      rotate: 0.5deg;
    }
    .deck img:nth-child(4) {
      rotate: 3deg;
    }
    .deck img:nth-child(5) {
      rotate: 6.5deg;
    }
    /* The card currently in focus, set on a timer by the script below. */
    .deck img.is-front {
      z-index: 3;
      transform: translateY(-0.5rem) scale(1.08);
      box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgb(0 0 0 / 20%);
      filter: saturate(1);
    }
    /* Hover and keyboard focus always win over the timer. */
    .deck img:hover,
    .deck img:focus-visible {
      z-index: 4;
      transform: translateY(-0.75rem) scale(1.11);
      box-shadow: 0 10px 28px rgb(0 0 0 / 24%);
      filter: saturate(1);
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .deck img,
      .deck img.is-front,
      .deck img:hover,
      .deck img:focus-visible {
        transform: none;
        transition: none;
      }
    }
    @media (max-width: 34rem) {
      .deck img + img {
        margin-left: -1.25rem;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <script is:inline>
    (() => {
      const deck = document.querySelector('.deck');
      if (!deck) return;
      const cards = Array.from(deck.querySelectorAll('img'));
      if (cards.length < 2) return;

      const reduced = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
      let i = 0;
      let timer = null;

      const show = (n) => {
        cards.forEach((c, idx) => c.classList.toggle('is-front', idx === n));
      };

      const start = () => {
        if (timer || reduced.matches) return;
        timer = setInterval(() => {
          i = (i + 1) % cards.length;
          show(i);
        }, 2600);
      };
      const stop = () => {
        clearInterval(timer);
        timer = null;
      };

      show(0);
      if (!reduced.matches) start();

      // Pause while a visitor is interacting, and when the tab is hidden.
      deck.addEventListener('pointerenter', stop);
      deck.addEventListener('pointerleave', start);
      deck.addEventListener('focusin', stop);
      deck.addEventListener('focusout', start);
      document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', () =>
        document.hidden ? stop() : start()
      );
      reduced.addEventListener('change', () => (reduced.matches ? stop() : start()));
    })();
  </script>
</Base>
